{
  "_schema_version": 1,
  "env_id": "PullCubeTool-v1",
  "roles": {
    "movable": "actor:l_shape_tool",
    "destination": "actor:cube",
    "reference": "actor:table-workspace"
  },
  "notes": [
    "No goal entity exists; success is the cube's coordinate passing a threshold. planar-distance(cube, table-workspace) is a proxy: the table origin sits at XY ~(-0.12, 0), essentially the robot base, so the cube closing on it is the pull making progress. Dense signal only, never a success detector -- the environment's dense reward remains responsible for completion. If TableSceneBuilder moves the table origin this clause silently stops meaning anything.",
    "support-compatibility(cube, l_shape_tool) is deliberately absent: the support bucket was excluded at 15.7% presence, so no components back it and it would score unobserved forever.",
    "height-offset is not used for the pull: the cube slides along the table, so its height never changes."
  ],
